WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.222
Rhetorical Synthesis

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.724
Read the goal first. The notes come last.

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.015
How to spot it

00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:10.214
A bulleted list of notes

00:00:10.764 --> 00:00:13.271
The question says “the student wants to…”

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:17.847
It’s testing: choosing information for a specific job

00:00:19.047 --> 00:00:19.813
The method

00:00:20.213 --> 00:00:23.230
Step 1: Read the question first

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.975
Skip the notes for now.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.086
Step 2: Underline the goal

00:00:28.366 --> 00:00:30.161
The action and what it’s about.

00:00:30.711 --> 00:00:32.625
Step 3: Make a checklist

00:00:32.905 --> 00:00:36.383
Two bridges? A difference? About length?

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.303
Step 4: Tick every box

00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:41.758
Only one choice does the whole job.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.402
In a few words

00:00:43.552 --> 00:00:46.685
Goal. Checklist. Tick every box.

00:00:47.885 --> 00:00:48.778
Goal words

00:00:49.178 --> 00:00:50.171
Similarity

00:00:50.451 --> 00:00:52.502
Both items + what they share.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:53.801
Difference

00:00:54.081 --> 00:00:56.080
Both items + how they differ.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.276
Unfamiliar audience

00:00:58.556 --> 00:01:00.542
Explain the unfamiliar term.

00:01:01.092 --> 00:01:02.446
Aim, method, finding

00:01:02.726 --> 00:01:07.281
Aim = why. Method = how. Finding = what they found.

00:01:08.481 --> 00:01:09.542
Let’s try one

00:01:09.942 --> 00:01:13.944
The Akashi Kaikyō Bridge in Japan opened in 1998.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:18.641
Its central span is 1,991 meters long.

00:01:19.021 --> 00:01:23.343
The Golden Gate Bridge in the United States opened in 1937.

00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:27.587
Its central span is 1,280 meters long.

00:01:27.967 --> 00:01:29.777
Both are suspension bridges.

00:01:30.327 --> 00:01:34.671
While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

00:01:34.671 --> 00:01:40.051
The student wants to emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two bridges’ central spans.

00:01:40.051 --> 00:01:45.788
Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:51.184
The goal: emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two spans.

00:01:51.184 --> 00:01:54.749
Your checklist: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:59.445
Cross out A, a similarity; B, a difference in dates;

00:01:59.445 --> 00:02:01.871
and D, which mentions only one bridge.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:06.536
C ticks every box: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:02:07.736 --> 00:02:08.805
Common traps

00:02:09.205 --> 00:02:10.501
True but off-task

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:12.805
Accurate, but does a different job.

00:02:13.355 --> 00:02:14.271
Half the goal

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.635
Ticks one box, misses another.

00:02:17.835 --> 00:02:19.458
Rhetorical Synthesis

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.870
Goal. Checklist. Tick every box.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.000
Spot it

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.851
Bulleted notes + “The student wants to…”

00:02:27.401 --> 00:02:28.108
Steps

00:02:28.308 --> 00:02:30.161
1. Read the question first

00:02:30.441 --> 00:02:31.954
2. Underline the goal

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.683
3. Make a checklist

00:02:33.963 --> 00:02:36.364
4. Pick the choice that ticks every box

00:02:36.914 --> 00:02:37.639
Remember

00:02:37.839 --> 00:02:41.296
Similarity: both items + what they share

00:02:41.576 --> 00:02:44.674
Difference: both items + how they differ

00:02:44.954 --> 00:02:47.573
New audience: explain the term

00:02:47.853 --> 00:02:51.099
Aim = why, method = how, finding = result

00:02:51.649 --> 00:02:52.090
Trap

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.981
True, but does a different job

00:02:54.731 --> 00:02:58.149
